$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1: To a microwave vial were added
7-chloro-1-{[(2S)-3,3-dimethylbutan-2-yl]amino}-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide
(500 mg, 1.45 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (589 mg, 2.32 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (133 mg, 0.15 mmol), tricyclohexylphosphine (81 mg, 0.29 mmol),
and potassium acetate (356 mg, 3.62 mmol). Degassed dioxane (10 mL) was
added and the mixture was heated by microwave irradiation to a 150°C for
1 h. The reaction was cooled to room temperature, diluted with ethyl
acetate, and filtered through Celite. The solid was washed several times
with ethyl acetate and the filtrate was concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
to afford
1-{[(2S)-3,3-dimethylbutan-2-yl]amino}-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide.
Yellow solid, yield 467 mg, 1.07 mmol, 74%. LRMS (ESI) calc'd for
C24H34BN4O3 [M+H]+ 437.3, found 437.2. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CD3OD) δ 8.46 (s,
1H), 8.04 (s, 1H), 7.90 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.70 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H),
4.47 (dd, J = 6.6, 13.2 Hz, 1H), 1.36 (s, 12H), 1.29 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H),
1.06 (s, 9H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, microwave vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 1-Amino-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indol-4-carboxamide Inhibitors of
Janus Kinase 2 (JAK2) for the Treatment of Myeloproliferative Disorders
