$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-(((3S,3aS)-1-oxo-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide
(34). A mixture of 5 (1.0 g, 2.93 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (0.89 g,
3.52 mmol), potassium acetate (0.86 g, 8.79 mmol) and
1,1-[bis-(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene]dichloropalladium(II)
dichloromethane complex (0.24 g, 0.29 mmol) in DMSO (16 mL) was degassed
and flushed with argon. The mixture was hearted at 80 °C for 1 h. Ethyl
acetate (150 mL) was added, and the mixture was filtered through Celite,
washed with saturated brine, dried over sodium sulfate, and evaporated.
The dark residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel with
petroleum/ ethyl acetate (1:1) to give 34.
N-(((3S,3aR)-1-oxo-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)acetamide(92).
Compound 92 (1.6 g, 74%) was yielded from 91 (1.9 g, 5.6 mmol) in the
same manner as described for 34. Mp: 210-212°C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6)
δ 8.20 (s, 1H), 7.94 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (dd, J1 = 8.1, J2=1.4 Hz,
1H), 7.17 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 1H), 4.86 (td, J1 = 8.7, J2=4.3 Hz, 1H), 4.61
(dd, J1 = 10.4, J2=3.0 Hz, 1H), 4.39 - 4.31 (m, 1H), 4.07 (t, J = 10.4
Hz, 1H), 3.51 - 3.42 (m, 1H), 3.32-3.23 (m, 1H), 1.85 (s, 3H), 1.28 (s,
12H); MS (EI) m/z: 388[M]+.
