$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (a) 6-(2-Furyl)pyrazin-2-amine General Method
A: Suzuki Couplings An oven dried resealable Schlenk tube was charged
with 6-chloropyrazin-2-amine (0.73 g, 5.7 mmol), an aromatic boronic acid
(7.4 mmol), dioxane (50 mL) and a 2M aqueous solution of cesium carbonate
3 (8.5 mL, 17.1 mmol). The Schlenk tube was subjected to three cycles of
evacuation-backfilling with argon, and
1,1'-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene-palladium(II) dichloride
dichloromethane complex (PdCl2dppf) (0.29 g, 0.35 mmol) was added. After
three new cycles of evacuation-backfilling with argon, the Schlenk tube
was capped and stirred and heated to 90 °C. After 16h, the mixture was
cooled and partitioned between water and ethyl acetate and the aqueous
phase was extracted with further ethyl acetate. The combined organic
layer was washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and evaporated. The desired
product was obtained after purification of the residue by flash
chromatography. (a) 6-(2-Furyl)pyrazin-2-amine (c)
6-Pyridin-3-yl-5-pyridin-4-ylpyrazin-2-amine Obtained as a beige solid
(74%) from 5-bromo-6-pyridin-3-ylpyrazin-2-amine and
4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine following General
Method A. δ 1H NMR (CDCl3): 8.68 (dd, 1H), 8.61(dd, 1H), 8.53 (d, 2H),
8.11(s, 1H), 7.69 (dd, 1H), 7.26 (m, 3H), 4.93 (s, 2H). ESI/MS (m/e, %):
249 [(M+1)+, C14H11N5]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
