$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM PCPDTBT: [Scheme S2].S24,7-bis
(4,4,5,5,-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole
(0.0708 g, 0.182 mmol), bis-2,6-dibromo-4,4-bis
(2-ethylhexyl)-4H-cyclopenta (2,1-b:3,4-b') dithiophene (0.103 g, 0.184
mmol), and Aliquat336 (10 mg) were weighed in a two necked flask.
Ar-bubbled aqueous K2CO3 (2 M, 0.36 ml) and toluene (10 ml) were poured
into the flask. The remaining air was removed from the flask by applying
freeze-pump-thaw and the process was repeated three times. Pd(PPh3)4 (3.6
mg, 3.1 μmol) was added under Ar counter flow. The reaction mixture was
refluxed at 120 °C for 3 days. Bromobenzene (0.283 g, 1.8 mmol) was added
to the reaction mixture then 2 h later, phenylboronic acid pinacol ester
(0.404 g, 1.98 mmol) was added and it refluxed for 2 h to complete the
end capping reaction. The resulting polymer solution was diluted by
adding toluene (50 mL) and poured into Ar-bubbeld methanol under
stirring. The precipitate was filtered and dried in a vacuum oven. The
polymer was dissolved in chloroform and purified by column chromatography
(chloroform, NH and NH2 silica). Finally the concentrated chloroform
solution was poured into methanol, and the precipitate was collected by
filtration. Blue crude,yield (0.0712 g, 0.13 mmol,74 %). Mw = 1.08 × 104
g mol-1, PDI = 1.24.
