$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthetic Procedure for Compound 27 (Scheme
1A). A mixture of 10 mmol of thiourea (a) and 10 mmol of halogenated
ketone (b) was dissolved in 10 mL of 2-propanol. The formed solution was
refluxed for 4 h, and the organic solvent was removed under vacuum. The
residue was treated with 20 mL of brine and extracted with 30 mL of ethyl
acetate (2 times). Combined organic layer was dried with sodium sulfate,
filtered, and evaporated. The obtained solid was purified by preparative
HPLC (eluent EtOAc/hexane = 1/1).
(4-(4-methylthiophen-3-yl)thiazol-2-yl)morpholine (79). Yield: 73%.;
purity 98% by LCMS. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 400MHz): 2.37 (3H, s), 3.40-3.42
(4H, m), 3.72-3.7 (4H, m), 6.94 (1H, s), 7.19-7.20 (1H, m), 7.69-7.70
(1H, d). MS (ESI): m/z (M + H)+ 276.2.
