$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for Preparation of
Methoxo(5,10,15-tris(5,2':5',2"-terthien-2-yl)subporphyrinato)boron(III)
(5) To the mixture of 3 (40.1 mg, 53.0 μmol), 2,2'-bithiophene-5-boronic
acid pinacol ester (57.9 mg, 198 μmol), and Pd(PPh3)4 (9.2 mg, 15 mol%)
in a Schlenk tube, THF (1.0 ml), toluene (1.0 mL) and 2M K2CO3 (0.3 mL)
were added. The resulting solution was deoxygenated via three
freeze-pump-thaw cycles, and then refluxed for 3 days. The resulting
mixture was poured into a saturated solution of ammonium chloride and
extracted with CHCl3. The organic layer was washed with brine and dried
over Na2SO4. After the solvent was evaporated, the mixture was
chromatographed through a silica gel column (eluent:
dichloromethane/hexane = 2:1 to 1:0). Pure 5 was obtained by
recrystallization from CHCl3/MeOH as a purple solid (29.6 mg, 73%).
Methoxo(5,10,15-tris(5,2':5',2"-terthien-2-yl)subporphyrinato)boron(III)
(5), Yield (29.6 mg, 73%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CD2Cl4) δ 8.40 (s, 6H, β),
7.88 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 3H, Ha), 7.54 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 3H, Hb), 7.34 (d, J =
3.7, 3H, He), 7.31 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 3H, Hg), 7.29 (d, J = 3.7, 3H, Hc),
7.22 (d, J = 3.7, 3H, Hd), 7.12 (dd, J = 5.0 and 3.7 Hz, 3H, Hf), and
0.93 (s, 3H, axial-methoxy); 11B NMR (193 MHz, CDCl3) δ -14.5 (s, 1B);
13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 140.4, 139.7, 137.5, 136.7, 135.5, 131.7,
128.1, 125.0, 124.9, 124.8, 124.6, 124.0, 122.5, 113.9, and 46.9; HR-ESI
TOF-MS m/z = 979.9790 (calcd for C51H27B1N3S9 = 979.9788 [M - OMe]+);
UV-vis (in CH2Cl2) λ [nm](ε [M-1 cm-1]) 436(140000) and 572(51000).
Fluorescence (in CH2Cl2, λex = 436 nm); λmax [nm] = 714, ΦF = 0.17.
Crystallographic data for 5: C52H30B1N3O1S9, M = 1012.23, triclinic, P-1,
a = 14.900(4) Å , b = 18.725(6) Å , c = 19.242(6) Å , α = 113.171(9)°, β
= 111.245(9)°, γ = 95.232(10)°, V = 4426(2) Å 3, Z = 4, R1 = 0.0941 (for
I > 2σ(I)), wR2 = 0.2731 (for all data), GOF = 1.013, CCDC-784373.
