$DATUM 3,4'-Dihexyl-5-methyl-2,2'-bithiophene (20). A solution of 18 (2.8 g,
10.8 mmol),
2-(4-hexylthiophen-2-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (19, 3.5
g, 11.9mmol) and Cs2CO3 (10.6 g, 2.4 mmol) in toluene (50 mL) was
degassed for 10 min. Pd(PPh3)4 (0.63 g, 0.54 mmol) was added and the
resulting solution was vigorously refluxed overnight under inert
atmosphere. The solution was cooled to room temperature and diluted with
n-hexane, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting crude residue
was purified via flash chromatography (SiO2, n-hexane) to give 20 (2.8 g,
7.9 mmol, 73% yield) as a colourless oil. Rf 0.31 (n-hexane); IR (neat)
2927, 2856, 2283, 1540, 1461, 1377, 1218, 1201, 1132, 856, 831, 728, 646
cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.88 (d, J= 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (dd, J= 1.5, 0.5 Hz,
1H), 6.59 (d, J= 1.0 Hz, 1H), 2.70 - 2.64 (m, 2H), 2.63 - 2.57 (m, 2H),
2.44 (d, J= 1.0 Hz, 3H), 1.68 - 1.56 (m, 4H), 1.40 - 1.27 (m, 12H), 0.93
- 0.87 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 143.4, 139.3, 137.7, 136.2, 128.5,
128.3, 126.7, 119.3, 31.7, 31.7, 31.6, 30.7, 30.5, 30.4, 29.2, 29.2,
29.0, 22.7, 22.6, 15.2, 14.1, 14.1, 14.1; LRMS (EI): m/z (%): 192 (15),
193 (11), 207 (17), 208 (11). 221 (11), 277 (34), 278 (53), 279 (13), 291
(19), 348 (100), 349 (26), 350 (13); HRMS (EI): Calcd for C21H3232S2:
348.1945 [M]+·, found: 348.1938.
