$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-[3-(2-Chlorophenyl)-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta-[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl]methanesulfonamide
(37). A reaction vessel was charged with 12a (40.0 mg, 0.12 mmol),
2-chlorophenylboronic acid (22mg, 0.14mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (4.0mg,
0.004mmol), K2CO3 (50mg, 0.36mmol), and 1,4-dioxane (3mL). Themixture was
sparged with argon for 10 min and then heated to 100 °C overnight. The
reaction mixture was cooled to ambient temperature. The mixture was
diluted in EtOAc and washed withH2Oand saturated aqueousNH4Cl. The
organic layer was separated and dried over MgSO4. The solution was
filtered, concentrated in vacuo, and purified by reverse phase HPLC
(40-100% CH3CN/H2O with 0.05% TFA) to afford 35 mg of 37 (71%).
N-[5-oxo-3-(1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl]methanesulfonamide
(46). Prepared using the method described for 37, using
4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole; 200 mg
(73%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 13.19 (s, 1H); 10.39 (s, 1H); 9.24 (d,
J = 1.8 Hz, 1H); 8.60 (s, 1H); 8.54 (s, 1H); 8.19 (s, 1H); 7.99 (d, J =
1.8 Hz, 1H); 7.77 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 7.58 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.8 Hz, 1H);
7.33 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1H); 7.24 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H); 3.07 (s, 3H). LRMS
(ESI) calc’d for (C18H15N4O3S) [M+ H]+, 367.1; found 366.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a 5H-Benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-5-one (MK-2461)
Inhibitor of c-Met Kinase for the Treatment of Cancer
