$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
trans-4-((2-(Butylamino)-5-(pyridin-3-yl)pyrimidin-4-yl)amino)cyclohexanol
(4) (General Procedure B) A mixture of lithium 3-pyridinyl trihydroborate
(74 mg, 0.5 mmol, 2.5 eq.), copper bromide (6.0 mg, 0.040 mmol, 0.2 eq.),
potassium carbonate (56 mg, 0.40 mmol, 2.0 eq.) and IIa (69 mg, 0.20
mmol, 1.0 eq) in DMF/H2O (2.0 mL/0.50 mL) was added PdCl2(dppf) (16.3 mg,
0.020 mmol, 0.1 eq.). The reaction mixture was heated at 120°C in the
open air for 30 min, and then cooled to room temperature. The solid was
removed by filtration through a short pad of celite (washed with DMF).
4-((2-(butylamino)-5-(5-chloropyridin-2-yl)pyrimidin-4-yl)amino)cyclohexanol
(94 mg, 0.25 mmol) (prepared based on general procedure B from
(5-chloropyridin-2-yl) trihydroxyborate lithium (3.246 g, 18.0 mmol, 3.0
eq.) as a brown solid (1.63 g, 73%). LC-MS, >98% purity. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD3OD) δ 8.71-8.57 (m, 1H), 8.33 (s, 1H), 7.96 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.5 Hz, 1H),
7.89 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 4.22-4.05 (m, 1H), 3.77-3.61 (m, 1H), 3.49 (s,
2H), 2.16 (d, J = 10.6 Hz, 2H), 2.08-1.95 (m, 2H), 1.67 (dt, J = 12.7,
7.6 Hz, 2H), 1.59-1.33 (m, 6H), 1.00 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H). LC-MS (ESI+):
tR = 4.809 min, MS m/z 376.0 [M+1]+.
