$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method C: Suzuki-Coupling. The corresponding
benzene derivative and the boronic acid were dissolved in toluene (20 mL)
and aq. Na2CO3 (2.0 M, 5.0 mL). The mixture was deoxygenated under
reduced pressure and flushed with N2. After having repeated this cycle
three times, Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mol%) was added, and the resulting suspension
was heated under reflux for 8 h. After cooling, the phases were separated
and the water phase was extracted two times with ethyl acetate. The
combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by flash chromatography
on silica-gel, using 5 % methanol in ethyl acetate.
2-Furan-3-yl-5-imidazol-1-ylmethyl-pyridine (40). Synthesized using
3-furanylboronic acid (188 mg, 1.68 mmol) and 1a (200 mg, 0.84 mmol)
according to Method C. Brown solid. Yield: 144 mg, 0.61 mmol, 73 %. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δH (ppm): 5.13 (s, 2H), 6.87 (dd, J = 1.9, 0.9 Hz,
1H), 6.90 (t, J = 1.3 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (s, 1H), 7.41 (dd, J = 8.2, 2.2 Hz,
1H), 7.43 (dd, J = 8.2, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (t, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (brs,
1H), 8.02 (dd, J = 0.7 Hz, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz): δC
(ppm) = 48.10, 108.5, 118.9, 120.1, 126.5, 129.5, 130.3, 135.6, 137.3,
141.5, 144.0, 148.6, 152.1; MS (ESI): m/z = 226.15 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
