$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a dried flask were added compound 1a-II
(3.66 g, 12.8 mmol), 2-bromo-3-methylpyridine (2.8 mL, d = 1.544, 25.5
mmol), Cs2CO3 (5.70 g, 38.4 mmol), and Pd(dppf)Cl2·CH2Cl2 (612.9 mg,
0.075 mmol, 5 mol%) in dioxane (150 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere. The
resulting mixture was stirred at 80°C for 39 h, then filtered through
celite, washed with ethyl acetate, and evaporated to afford the crude
product. Flash chromatograph (eluent: toluene/ethyl acetate = 1.5/1 to
hexane/ethyl acetate = 1/2) afforded compound 1a: Red solid. The reaction
of 1b-II (164.3 mg, 0.57 mmol), 2-bromopyridine (109 μL, 180.6 mg, 1.14
mmol, d = 1.657,), Cs2CO3 (254.9 mg, 1.7 mmol), and Pd(dppf)Cl2·CH2Cl2
(33.1 mg, 0.4 mmol, 7 mol%) in dioxane (4 mL). 1b (99.4 mg, 73%) (flash
chromatograph eluent: hexane/ethyl acetate = 1/1 to 1/2): Red solid.
1-methyl-4-(pyridin-2-yl)-isatin 1b. (zr-3-36, 44) mp: 187-189°C; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.77 – 8.69 (m, 1H), 7.84-7.78 (m, 2 H, Ar-H), 7.68
(t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H, Ar-H), 7.52 (dd, J 1 = 8.0 Hz, J 1 = 0.9 Hz, 1 H,
Ar-H), 7.39-7.31 (m, 1 H, Ar-H), 6.94 (dt, J 1 = 8.0 Hz, J 1 = 0.9 Hz, 1
H, Ar-H), 3.30 (s, 3 H, CH3); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 182.0, 157.6,
153.2, 151.9, 149.7, 141.0, 137.9, 136.0, 125.8, 124.8, 123.6, 113.7,
109.7, 26.3; IR ν (neat, cm-1) 3059, 1737, 1589, 1566, 1460, 1431, 1357,
1321, 1205, 1102, 1090; HRMS (CI) for C14H10N2O2 (MW = 238, M+):
238.0742. Found: 238.0744.
