$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Indole-amine 15 A round-bottomed flask was charged with 7 (89 mg, 0.31
mmol), indole-2-boronic acid pinacol ester (14, 92 mg, 0.37 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (14.0 mg, 0.031 mmol), P(o-tol)3 (18.2 mg, 0.062 mmol), and
Na2CO3 (130 mg, 1.24 mmol), fitted with a rubber septum, evacuated, and
then backfilled with Ar. Freshly degassed THF/H2O (10:1, 3.1 mL) was
added to the flask, and the reaction mixture was stirred for 15 h at room
temperature. After the reaction mixture was eluted with a short column of
silica gel (flash, EtOAc/CHCl3 = 1/9), the solvent was evaporated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel flash column
chromatography (EtOAc/CHCl3 = 1/9). Indole-amine 15 (63 mg, 73%) as a
yellow solid. 15: UV (MeOH) λ max nm: 391.0, 283.0, 264.0, 216.0. IR νmax
(ATR) cm-1: 3293, 2923, 1624, 1559. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ ppm: 10.45
(1H, br s), 7.54 (1H, d, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.40 (1H, d, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.16 (1H,
dd, J = 8.1, 8.1 Hz), 7.08 (1H, dd, J = 8.1, 8.1 Hz), 6.54 (1H, d, J =
1.8 Hz), 6.46 (1H, br s), 6.32 (1H, td, J = 4.8, 1.8 Hz), 5.05 (1H, m),
3.45 (2H, m), 2.50 (2H, m), 1.62 (3H, d, J = 6.6 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100
MHz) δ ppm: 166.8, 148.4, 135.1, 132.4, 130.7, 128.5, 128.1, 121.6,
119.7, 119.3, 111.1, 99.3, 89.0, 72.7, 38.5, 24.4, 18.9. ESI-MS m/z: 281
[M+H]+, 303 [M+Na]+. HRESI-MS: calcd. for C17H17N2O2 [M+H]+ 281.1290;
found 281.1293. [α]D 24 -4.6 (c 0.37, CHCl3).
