$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 4 (GP4) Following the method
of Alvarez-Bua,26 aminide 7c or 9b (1.0 equiv), the corresponding boronic
acid (1.5 equiv) and K2CO3 (10.0 equiv) were combined in a
toluene/ethanol mixture (4:1, 15 mL/mmol). Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mol %) was added
and the mixture was stirred under argon at 80 °C for 4.5 h. Once the
starting material were consumed (detected by TLC) the solution was
filtered and concentrated. The crude residue was purified by flash
chromatography and used as detailed below in the subsequent catalysis.
Following GP4 using (3-formylphenyl)boronic acid (143 mg, 0.90 mmol) and
7c (190 mg, 0.63 mmol). After purification by flash chromatography [ethyl
acetate:methanol (8:2)] aminide 7b was isolated.
N-(5-(2-Bromopyridin-5-yl)pyrimidin-2-yl)pyridinium aminide (9c)
Following GP4 using (6-bromopyridin-3-yl)boronic acid (242 mg, 1.20
mmol). After purification by flash chromatography [ethyl acetate:methanol
(7:3)] aminide 9c was isolated as a bright yellow solid (191 mg, 73%).
~90% purity (estimated by 1H NMR); mp: 221-222 °C; 1 (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
8.82 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 8.46 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 8.40 (s, 2H), 7.83
(app. t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.68-7.57 (m, 3H), 7.48 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H);
13C-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 167.3, 155.9, 146.5, 142.7 (2xC), 139.7,
135.0, 134.8, 131.7, 128.1 (2xC), 126.2 (2xC), 116.8; IR νmax/cm-1 3130,
3014, 1572, 1498, 1352, 1183, 1074, 957, 1052, 864, 795; HRMS (ES-TOF):
m/z: calcd. for C14H11N579Br: 328.0197, found: 328.0198 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Direct Route into Fused Imidazo-diazines and Imidazo-pyridines Using
Nucleophilic Nitrenoids in a Gold-Catalyzed Formal [3 + 2]-Dipolar
Cycloaddition
