$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1: To
7-chloro-1-{[(1R)-1-cyclopropyl-2,2,2-trifluoroethyl]amino}-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide
(250 mg, 0.65 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (60 mg, 0.065 mmol),
tricyclohexylphosphine (37 mg, 0.131 mmol) and potassium acetate (160 mg,
1.63 mmol) in dioxane (3.3 mL) was added bispinacolatodiboron (265 mg,
1.045 mmol). The reaction solution was purged with nitrogen for 5 minutes
and heated to 100 °C for 16 h. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature and diluted with ethyl acetate. The mixture was filtered
through a Celite pad and washed with ethyl acetate. The filtrate was
concentrated under reduced pressure and the residue purified by
chromatography on silica gel to afford
1-{[(1H)-1-cyclopropyl-2,2,2-trifluoroethyl]amino}-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide.
Light brown solid, yield 225 mg, 0.47 mmol, 73%. LRMS (ESI) calc'd for
(C23H27BF3N4O3) [M + H]+ 475.2, found 475.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 1-Amino-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indol-4-carboxamide Inhibitors of
