$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure C: Purification by flash
column chromatography On the bench-top, into a 10 mL screw vial (46 x
22.5) the Pd catalyst, aryl-halide, MIDA boronate, and Teflon® stir bar
were added to the vial that was then capped. The vial was briefly
degassed with Argon for less than 1 min. The base was then added followed
by 2 wt % TPGS-750-M/H2O via syringe. The vial top was wrapped using
Parafilm® and allowed to stir vigorously at RT for 16-24 h. Upon
completion, 5 mL of 26.5g/g aq. NaCl was added to the vial and stirring
continued. The contents were then transferred to a separatory funnel and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 25 mL). The organic phases were collected and
the solvent was removed via rotary evaporation at <100 torr, with the
water bath temperature at or under 40 °C. The crude material was then
loaded onto a Biotage® samplet and fitted on top of a pre-packed Biotage®
KP-Sil cartridge. The eluent was an EtOAc/heptane mixture. The solvent
was removed via rotary evaporation at <100 torr, with the water bath
temperature at or under 40 °C, affording the desired product. Note: The
amount of silica gel and solvent required in the extraction and
purification steps were NOT optimized. Synthesis of
1-benzyl-4-(p-tolyl)-1H-pyrazole (Scheme 2) The title compound was
obtained according to the general procedure C: (dtbpf)PdCl2 (6.6 mg, 2.0
mol %), 1-benzyl-4-bromo-1H-pyrazole (118.6 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv),
4-tolylboronic acid MIDA ester (123.5 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv), Et3N (210
μL, 1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv), and 2 wt % TPGS-750-M/H2O (1 mL, 0.5 M). The
crude product was purified by the Biotage® using a 10 g pre-packed
cartridge and 1 g samplet. The desired compound as an off-white powder
(105.4 mg, 85% yield). Synthesis of ethyl (4-(methylthio)phenyl)carbamate
(Scheme 3) The title compound was obtained according to the general
procedure C: (40 °C), (dtbpf)PdCl2 (13.0 mg, 4.0 mol %), 5-chloroindole
(75.8 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv), 2-benzofuranylboronic acid MIDA ester
(163.8 mg, 0.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv), Et3N (210 μL, 1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv), and
2 wt % TPGS-750-M/H2O (1 mL, 0.5 M). The crude product was purified by
the Biotage® using a 10 g pre-packed cartridge and 1 g samplet. The
desired compound as a yellowish powder (84 mg, 72% yield). TLC: 10%
EtOAc/heptane. Rf = 0.15, UV active 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.25 (br
s, 1H), 8.21 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 7.73 (dd, J = 1.5, 8.5 Hz, 1H),
7.59-7.52 (m, 2H), 7.46 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.28-7.20 (m, 3H), 6.97 (d,
J = 1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.65-6.64 (m, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, Suzuki-Miyaura coupling, micellar catalysis
used, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
